{
  "bio": [
    "Grendene Bartelle cofounded his eponymous company Grendene, one of the world's largest sandal manufacturers, with his twin brother Alexandre.",
    "He is vice chairman of the board of directors at Grendene and owns just under 14% of the Sao Paulo-listed company.",
    "Grendene Bartelle invests in other companies such as footwear maker Vulcabras, where he serves as chairman and holds a 50% stake.",
    "His son Pedro runs Vulcabras as its CEO."
  ],
  "about": [
    "Grendene Bartelle is married to Tania Bulhoes, a Brazilian entrepreneur who owns Tania Bulhoes Perfumes Ltda., a well known retailer of perfumes, creams and soaps."
  ]
}